<newsitem itemid="50801" id="root" date="1996-09-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Britain's APV H1 pretax profits slide.</title>
<headline>Britain's APV H1 pretax profits slide.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.2		    vs 1.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.0		    vs 1.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.7		    vs 7.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   346.1		  vs 401.1</p>
<p> Operating result  loss 6.0		    vs 12.6 profit</p>
<p> Exceptional costs	8.0		    vs nil</p>
<p> Exceptional profit     8.7		    vs 2.0 loss</p>
<p> Interest		   2.0		    vs 2.7</p>
<p> Tax			  0.2		    vs 2.1</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.5		    vs 5.0</p>
<p> Retained loss	    2.5		    vs 1.9 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 3, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1</p>
<p>NOTE-- APV Plc chairman Sir Peter Cazalet said in a statement &quot;There are signs that order intake is picking up. This, combined with the benefit of accumulated cost savings, means that the group continues to expect progress in the second half of the year compared with the second half of 1995.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
